WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.820
If you can't decide between visiting Japan

00:00:01.821 --> 00:00:03.461
or South Korea for your next trip,

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:06.661
I'm here to help you after visiting both countries in the last year.

00:00:06.662 --> 00:00:08.421
If you're on a budget, go to Korea.

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:10.461
While food is pretty affordable in both countries,

00:00:10.462 --> 00:00:13.521
transportation and accommodation are generally cheaper in Korea.

00:00:13.522 --> 00:00:14.741
If you're a solo traveler,

00:00:14.742 --> 00:00:16.581
both countries are extremely safe,

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.581
but I'd say probably go to Japan

00:00:18.582 --> 00:00:21.341
for example. Solo dining is extremely common in Japan,

00:00:21.342 --> 00:00:22.861
so you'll never feel out of place,

00:00:22.862 --> 00:00:26.661
whereas in Korea the local cuisine is usually intended for sharing,

00:00:26.662 --> 00:00:28.761
which can be more difficult for solo travelers.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.261
However, if you like meeting and interacting with locals,

00:00:31.262 --> 00:00:33.021
I'd probably say Korea is better.

00:00:33.022 --> 00:00:35.261
In Japan people tend to keep to themselves a lot,

00:00:35.262 --> 00:00:37.821
so I found it a bit difficult to interact with locals,

00:00:37.822 --> 00:00:41.021
whereas in Korea despite despite not speaking any English either,

00:00:41.022 --> 00:00:44.061
I found people who were a bit more open and curious with foreigners

00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:45.861
and I had lovely interactions.

00:00:45.862 --> 00:00:46.461
And especially

00:00:46.462 --> 00:00:49.421
the younger people would approach us and want to speak to us

00:00:49.422 --> 00:00:50.781
just to practice their English,

00:00:50.782 --> 00:00:52.101
which was super endearing.

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:54.421
Having said that, if you're a Westerner like me

00:00:54.422 --> 00:00:56.521
and you want to travel somewhere that feels

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.300
vastly different from our culture,

00:00:58.301 --> 00:01:00.861
go to Japan. Korea is more influenced by western culture,

00:01:00.862 --> 00:01:02.981
so while it's still very different,

00:01:02.982 --> 00:01:05.621
it still feels more familiar than Japan in some ways.

00:01:05.622 --> 00:01:07.981
Or maybe you want that familiarity when you travel,

00:01:07.982 --> 00:01:09.621
and in that case, Go to Korea.

00:01:09.622 --> 00:01:11.661
And finally, if you want to visit somewhere

00:01:11.662 --> 00:01:14.621
and come back feeling like you saw all the main points,

00:01:14.622 --> 00:01:16.621
go to Korea. I spent three weeks in Korea,

00:01:16.622 --> 00:01:18.701
and I felt like I was able to get a sense

00:01:18.702 --> 00:01:20.721
for all the different areas of the country,

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:24.900
including Jeju Island. But Japan is gigantic.

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:27.181
I traveled across Japan for five weeks,

00:01:27.182 --> 00:01:30.161
and I still feel like I haven't seen anything.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.340
In fact, I'm going back to Japan next year again.

00:01:33.341 --> 00:01:35.861
So keep in mind that if you visit Japan,

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.101
you probably will want to go back.

00:01:38.102 --> 00:01:40.301
I hope this was helpful, and if you have more questions,

00:01:40.302 --> 00:01:42.965
let me know in the comments and I can answer in a part two.
